Fix an allocation leak in the HTTP/2 backlog tracking on stream reset

Backport of upstream commit 2a5ec806971627943db18601203129d9c58d959f for
AIKIDO-2026-915093. When an HTTP/2 stream that is waiting in the connection
window backlog is reset (or replaced by a RecycledStream), its reserved and/or
granted connection-level flow-control allocation was not returned to the
connection window nor removed from the backlog size tracking. Repeated stream
resets therefore leaked the connection flow-control window, eventually stalling
all streams on the connection (denial of service).

